---
/* The About shell.

   Exists so the nav's two-page behaviour is real and testable — the
   spec asks for exactly that and nothing more. About's own sections
   (stats, board, the CEO quote, the Journey Wall) come later, after
   the homepage.

   Note it does NOT place a [data-nav-dark-end] marker, so it gets a
   solid nav from the first paint. When its photographic banner is
   built, the banner opts in by placing that marker at the end of its
   dark region — the nav state follows the composition, not the page.
*/
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About bKash — Financial freedom for millions"
  description="A secure digital account where millions store value and decide how to use it."
  current="company"
>
  <main class="shell">
    <div class="wrap shell__in">
      <p class="t-eyebrow">About bKash</p>
      <h1 class="t-h1">Empowering 85M Bangladeshis with financial freedom</h1>
      <p class="t-lead">
        Bridging the everyday economy and digital finance, bKash brought millions into the
        formal economy who now have controls on their own money.
      </p>
      <p class="t-body">
        This page is a shell. It proves the nav renders its current state on a second page and
        that the Support button is present on both, which the prototype's hand-duplicated markup
        got wrong (audit A7).
      </p>
      <blockquote class="t-quote shell__quote">
        The pull-quote step exists for the CEO quote, which was the least-designed moment on the
        page. This is a placeholder using it, not the quote itself.
      </blockquote>
      <p class="t-sm shell__link">
        <a href="/">Back to the homepage</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>

<style>
  .shell {
    padding-top: calc(var(--nav-h) + var(--s-8));
    padding-bottom: var(--s-10);
  }

  .shell__in > * + * {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  .shell__quote {
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
    padding-inline-start: var(--s-5);
    border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--pink);
    color: var(--ink-2);
  }

  .shell__link {
    margin-top: var(--s-6);
  }
</style>
